Helios patch 0001 write-bytes-memcpy (netcode 1.4.8; WP-0.13r, NS-0.2 headroom)

netcode_write_bytes copied its input one byte at a time through netcode_write_uint8. netcode_write_packet
writes every payload packet's data with it before encrypting the packet in place, so the loop runs once per
payload byte of every packet a client or server sends. In a -fPIC build (CMake's position-independent code
for the static library) GCC does not inline netcode_write_uint8, an external function that could be
interposed, so every byte cost a call; inlined (Clang, MSVC) it is still a byte loop, because a store
through the uint8_t ** may alias the pointer it advances. In the NS-0.2 encrypted-stack benchmark
(700-byte EVENT_U messages, net_bench --stack) the loop took 11 % of the CPU per packet on Linux (GCC 13,
RelWithDebInfo; perf record, WP-0.13r). This patch copies with one memcpy and advances the pointer by the
same amount. No call site passes overlapping buffers (they copy between packet buffers and token or packet
structs), and a count of zero or less writes nothing, as the loop did, so the bytes written and the wire
format are unchanged.

Rebase notes: netcode_write_bytes keeps its signature; netcode_read_bytes still loops (it only reads
connect and challenge tokens, never payload packets, which netcode_read_packet copies with memcpy).

Upstream status: not submitted. Rebase on every netcode bump (K10), and delete the patch once upstream
copies with memcpy. Licence: MIT (Helios); netcode itself is BSD-3.

diff --git a/netcode.c b/netcode.c
index 6458cab..6b3d046 100755
--- a/netcode.c
+++ b/netcode.c
@@ -974,10 +974,13 @@ void netcode_write_uint64( uint8_t ** p, uint64_t value )
 
 void netcode_write_bytes( uint8_t ** p, uint8_t * byte_array, int num_bytes )
 {
-    int i;
-    for ( i = 0; i < num_bytes; i++ )
+    // Helios patch write-bytes-memcpy: one memcpy instead of one netcode_write_uint8 call per byte. Every
+    // payload packet passes through here before it is encrypted, and the byte loop cost 11 % of NS-0.2's
+    // encrypted-stack CPU per packet (WP-0.13r profile, GCC, -fPIC: the per-byte call is not inlined).
+    if ( num_bytes > 0 )
     {
-        netcode_write_uint8( p, byte_array[i] );
+        memcpy( *p, byte_array, (size_t) num_bytes );
+        *p += num_bytes;
     }
 }
 
